Since  $4\cdot\mathop{\text{lcm}}[m,10^{10}]$ divides $\mathop{\text{lcm}}[8m,10^{10}]$, let $k=\mathop{\text{lcm}}[m,10^{10}]$. Then:

\begin{align*}
\mathop{\text{lcm}}[8m,10^{10}] & = 4\cdot k\\
\mathop{\text{lcm}}[8,10^{10}] & = 80\cdot 10^{10}\\
\implies k & \leq \frac{80\cdot 10^{10}}{8} =10^{10}
\end{align*}

Thus, for $k$ to be the least possible, we need $k =10^{10}$, and this leads to:

